	<p><img src=3D"https://everymac.com/images/cpu_pictures/apple_imac_snow.gi=
f" alt=3D"Apple iMac G3 Graphite Snow Summer 2001" width=3D"209" height=3D"=
120" class=3D"comppic">The Apple iMac G3/600 (Summer 2001) features a 600 M=
Hz PowerPC 750cx (G3) processor with a 256k on-chip level 2 cache, 256 MB o=
f RAM, a 40.0 GB Ultra ATA hard drive, a slot loading 8X/4X/24X CD-RW drive=
, ATI Rage 128 Ultra (AGP 2X) graphics with 16 MB of VRAM, a Harman-Kardon =
designed sound system, and Firewire "400" ports packed into a translucent "=
graphite" or "snow" all-in-one case design with a 15-inch CRT display.<br><=
br>On January 7, 2002, Apple dropped the price from US$1299 to US$999 and b=
egan shipping the systems with MacOS X 10.1 selected as the default operati=
ng system, although MacOS 9 also was pre-installed.<br><br><i>Please note t=
hat Apple decided to refer to this line as the "Summer 2001" series, which =
refers to Summer in the Northern Hemisphere.</i><br><br>Also see: <a href=
=3D"https://everymac.com/systems/apple/imac/faq/differences-between-final-s=
ummer-2001-imac-g3.html">What</a> are the differences between the final "Su=
mmer 2001" iMac G3 models? </p>
=09
	<p><em>Despite the age of this system, site sponsor <a rel=3D"nofollow" hr=
ef=3D"https://everymac.com/owc" target=3D"_blank">Other World Computing</a>=
  has RAM, hard drives, SSDs, and other upgrades available for <a rel=3D"no=
follow" href=3D"https://eshop.macsales.com/MyOWC/Upgrades.cfm?model=3D372" =
target=3D"_blank">this specific iMac</a> while supplies last.</em></p>
